<title>USA: Amdahl Q3 shr loss $0.04 vs profit.</title>
<headline>Amdahl Q3 shr loss $0.04 vs profit.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMDAHL CORPORATION (AMEX: AMH)</p>
<p> Three Months Ended		Sep 27, 1996	Sep 29, 1995</p>
<p> Revenues			   $ 439,819,000     $ 350,016,000</p>
<p> Income (Loss) Before Taxes     (4,201,000)	  25,707,000</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)		  (4,833,000)	  20,057,000</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding(1)  120,881,000	 120,603,000</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss) Per Share(1)	 (.04)		   .17</p>
<p>Nine Months Ended	     Sept. 27, 1996(2)  Sept. 29, 1995</p>
<p> Revenues			   1,139,701,000     1,100,208,000</p>
<p> Income (Loss) Before Taxes   (280,791,000)	  85,743,000</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)		(292,792,000)	  66,893,000</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding(1)  120,223,000	 120,267,000</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss) Per Share(1)	(2.44)		   .56</p>
<p>NOTE: (1) Fully diluted for 1995.</p>
<p>	    (2) For the nine months ended Sept. 27, 1996, the</p>
<p>loss before taxes, net loss, and loss per share reflect second quarter nonrecurring charges to reduce the book value of certain assets and write off in-process R&amp;D associated with a recent acquisition in the amount of $150.7 million, or $1.25 per share.</p>
